FUNCTION UNDER TEST:
Name: count_digits
Signature: uint8_t count_digits(uint8_t *number, uint8_t N)
Description: /**
 * @brief Count the number of significant digits in a big-endian digit array.
 *
 * Scans the array from most significant digit to find the first non-zero digit,
 * then calculates the count of digits from that position. Handles the special
 * case where all digits are zero by returning 1.
 *
 * @param number Pointer to array of digits in big-endian order (most significant
 *               digit at index 0). Must be a valid pointer if N > 0.
 * @param N Length of the digit array. If zero, the function returns 0.
 *
 * @return Number of significant digits (1 for zero, 0 for empty array).
 */
Dependencies: None

FUNCTION IMPLEMENTATION (REFERENCE ONLY - do NOT copy into test):
```c
// C program for the function called count_digits
// Contains target function implementation and dependency signatures

#include <stdint.h>
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>

// Target function implementation
uint8_t count_digits(uint8_t *number, uint8_t N)
{
    if (number == NULL || N == 0)
    {
        return 0;
    }

    uint8_t start_pos = N - 1;
    while (start_pos > 0 && number[start_pos] == 0) start_pos--;

    /* Handle case of all zeros */
    if (start_pos == 0 && number[0] == 0)
    {
        return 1;  /* Zero has 1 digit */
    }

    return start_pos + 1;
}

```

